{"repositoryId":1362022062,"availability":"available","full":"AetherAI3/Predator","name":"Predator","description":"Gen3 Predator by Aether AI: Ai-quantum reasoning & Public Off-Sec training evidence.","category":"Developer tools","language":null,"stars":12,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-09T00:02:20Z","updated":"2026-10-17T12:03:58Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://aetherai3.github.io/Predator/","topics":["adaptive-compilation","aether-ai","ai-agents","ai-security","application-security","code-analysis","ctf","hackthebox","llm","multi-agent-systems","qiskit","quantum-computing","quantum-optimization","qubo","reproducible-research","security-research","software-assurance","threat-modeling","verification","vulnerability-research"],"demo":"https://aetherai3.github.io/Predator/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:44:37.627Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:44:37.627Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:44:37.627Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.672Z","stars":11,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T13:44:37.627Z","stars":12,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI security research, software repair, and authorized VM workflows.","Predator brings AI reasoning, persistent context, and reviewed tool use into security research and software repair. Its research engine, Crucible, works like a lockpick: it holds verified evidence steady, proposes candidate chains, checks them against the real software, and banks only supported results. A QUBO can rank the next test; the recorded solver and native result determine what actually ran and what was established. Quantum simulation or hardware is identified only for runs that used it.","This is the public feature showcase and evidence collection. The CLI and operator engines are private, with reviewed research access."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AetherAI3/Predator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5d684fbd03812a8db885b8dee6c79c40d1787917e00